cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SPARQLcirc: Native-SPARQL Provenance Circuits for Exact
  Probabilistic Query Evaluation
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. The
  paper describing the approach is under submission; this entry will be
  updated to point at it once it appears.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Jingcheng
    affiliation: University of Stuttgart
repository-code: https://github.com/0sidewalkenforcer0/SPARQLcirc
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  SPARQLcirc rewrites a SPARQL query so that an unmodified SPARQL 1.1
  engine materializes a single shared, content-addressed provenance
  circuit as ordinary RDF. The circuit is then compiled and
  weighted-model-counted for exact probabilistic query evaluation over a
  fragment that includes non-monotone OPTIONAL and MINUS and recursive
  property paths, without modifying the database engine.
keywords:
  - SPARQL
  - RDF
  - provenance
  - probabilistic databases
  - knowledge compilation
  - weighted model counting
